From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: setup.py: support building from a plain source tarball (no VCS)

build_py gathers per-module timestamps by running "pydates" (needs a
mercurial checkout -- and python2-era mercurial APIs at that) or
"pydates.git" (needs a .git directory).  A release/source tarball has
neither, so the build exits 1 before compiling anything.

When neither ../.git nor ../.hg exists, skip the VCS mining and use a
single workspace timestamp for all modules, honouring
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH when the build environment provides it.  This is
faithful to what the machinery achieves in practice anyway: the
per-file lookup keys are bytes while the lookups use str (py3
bit-rot), so every file already falls back to the workspace stamp.

diff --git a/src/setup.py b/src/setup.py
--- a/src/setup.py
+++ b/src/setup.py
@@ -1105,20 +1105,32 @@
 
                 if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(pwd, "../.git")):
                     pydates = "pydates.git"
+                elif not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(pwd, "../.hg")):
+                        # Tarball build: no VCS metadata to mine for
+                        # stable per-file dates ("pydates" needs a
+                        # mercurial checkout, "pydates.git" a git one).
+                        # Use a single workspace stamp for everything;
+                        # honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH for reproducibility.
+                        pydates = None
+                        self.timestamps[b"."] = float(
+                            os.environ.get("SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH",
+                                os.stat(os.path.join(
+                                    pwd, "setup.py")).st_mtime))
 
-                p = subprocess.Popen(
-                    os.path.join(pwd, pydates),
-                    stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
+                if pydates:
+                        p = subprocess.Popen(
+                            os.path.join(pwd, pydates),
+                            stdout=subprocess.PIPE)
 
-                for line in p.stdout:
-                        stamp, path = line.split()
-                        stamp = float(stamp)
-                        self.timestamps[path] = stamp
+                        for line in p.stdout:
+                                stamp, path = line.split()
+                                stamp = float(stamp)
+                                self.timestamps[path] = stamp
 
-                if p.wait() != 0:
-                        print("ERROR: unable to gather .py timestamps",
-                            file=sys.stderr)
-                        sys.exit(1)
+                        if p.wait() != 0:
+                                print("ERROR: unable to gather .py "
+                                    "timestamps", file=sys.stderr)
+                                sys.exit(1)
 
                 # Before building extensions, we need to generate .c files
                 # for the C extension modules by running the CFFI build
